                                        "entry_id": "a6416cd1-54bb-36ff-8eba-82f61c4408d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The role or state of being a mentor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c544a298-bcc0-4c91-8467-38732b295ca2",
                                                "sense_id": "d2e5be6b-506d-3bff-b3b9-5cf177eaf120",
                                                "text": "The mentorships were plenty, starting with Brian Derdall, a sort of rain-man genius in Engineering, along with T-man the technology guru, new hire peers Alex and Joel, and my new senior co-workers Ivan, Robert, and a sort of management mentor John."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2b07883-9a5f-4f8c-8445-4d3b6f44e127",
                                                "sense_id": "d2e5be6b-506d-3bff-b3b9-5cf177eaf120",
                                                "text": "In some mentorship programs, the mentees get a say in whom they will be paired with. A mentee may be drawn to make certain connections based on a sense of their professional influence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
